{{/*
  The front page. It is deliberately almost empty: enough that a fresh deployment
  has a working home rather than a 404, and little enough that replacing it is
  obviously the intended move.

  To make it yours, drop a pages/index.gohtml into TEMPLATE_DIR defining "content"
  — see the README's Theming section. Nothing here needs a fork or a rebuild.

  One thing to know before adding to it: this page is served outside the CSRF
  layer, because it carries no form and therefore sets no cookie. A form added here
  would be refused with a 403. Link to a page that has one — the product page and
  the cart both do.
*/}}
{{define "content"}}

<h1>{{.StoreName}}</h1>

{{/*
  Replace this line. It is deliberately plain rather than written for a shop that
  does not exist yet: made-up copy reads as finished, and the thing about copy that
  reads as finished is that nobody notices it shipping.
*/}}
<p class="lede muted">Welcome to {{.StoreName}}.</p>

{{/*
  A few of the newest products, as an example of what a front page can put here.
  The grid is the same one the catalog uses, so restyling a card changes both.
*/}}
{{if .Products}}
  <h2>New in</h2>
  {{template "product_grid" .}}
  <p class="see-all"><a href="/products" hx-boost="true">Browse all products →</a></p>
{{else}}
  <p class="muted">Nothing for sale yet.
    <a href="/products" hx-boost="true">The catalog</a> is where products appear.</p>
{{end}}

{{end}}
